  "description": "Heat shield (thermal protection system) design: ablative shields using PICA (Phenolic Impregnated Carbon Ablator) at 0.27 g/cm³ density surviving 2,900°C, SpaceX PICA-X variants targeting 10+ reuses, and reusable tiled TPS as flown on the Space Shuttle (LI-900 silica tiles). Selection trades ablation recession rate, peak heating flux (Apollo CM endured ~3,000 W/cm²), reusability, and areal mass against the entry trajectory's ballistic coefficient.",
